{
  "flow": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "width": 380,
        "height": 200,
        "id": "comment-multijudge",
        "type": "comment",
        "position": {"x": -420, "y": -120},
        "positionAbsolute": {"x": -420, "y": -120},
        "data": {
          "title": "Multi-Judge Agreement Flow",
          "text": "Three local models act as judges on the same response.\nPurpose: measure inter-judge agreement — do hermes3, phi4, and llama3.1 give consistent scores?\n\nFlow: Table of (task, response) pairs → 3 parallel judge prompts → Inspect comparison.\n\nHigh disagreement = unreliable single-judge scoring. Guides which judge model to trust for automated evals.\n\nMetric to compute manually: Cohen's kappa across the three judge columns."
        },
        "dragHandle": ".node-header"
      },
      {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 520,
        "id": "table-judgement",
        "type": "table",
        "position": {"x": -420, "y": 120},
        "positionAbsolute": {"x": -420, "y": 120},
        "data": {
          "title": "Responses to Judge",
          "columns": [
            {"header": "task", "key": "task"},
            {"header": "expected", "key": "expected"},
            {"header": "response", "key": "response"}
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "__uid": "j1",
              "task": "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many sheep are left?",
              "expected": "9",
              "response": "9 sheep are left. When 'all but 9 die', it means 9 survive."
            },
            {
              "__uid": "j2",
              "task": "A farmer has 17 sheep. All but 9 die. How many sheep are left?",
              "expected": "9",
              "response": "17 - 9 = 8 sheep are left."
            },
            {
              "__uid": "j3",
              "task": "Write a Python function is_palindrome(s) that handles None and mixed case.",
              "expected": "handles None, empty, case-insensitive",
              "response": "def is_palindrome(s):\n    if s is None:\n        return False\n    s = s.lower()\n    return s == s[::-1]"
            },
            {
              "__uid": "j4",
              "task": "Write a Python function is_palindrome(s) that handles None and mixed case.",
              "expected": "handles None, empty, case-insensitive",
              "response": "def is_palindrome(s):\n    return s == s[::-1]"
            },
            {
              "__uid": "j5",
              "task": "Summarize what Docker does in exactly 20 words. The word 'isolation' must appear.",
              "expected": "exactly 20 words, contains isolation",
              "response": "Docker packages applications with their dependencies into containers, providing isolation, portability, and consistent environments across development, testing, and production systems."
            },
            {
              "__uid": "j6",
              "task": "Summarize what Docker does in exactly 20 words. The word 'isolation' must appear.",
              "expected": "exactly 20 words, contains isolation",
              "response": "Docker uses isolation to run applications in containers, ensuring consistent behavior across different computing environments without conflicts."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
